# multi_assign.tkr — §9 F multiple assignment, array decomposition and multiple return, exercised end
# to end. The project's own `main.tks` build runs every form on the OWN-NATIVE backend and announces
# each case BY NAME (`scenario <name>: ok`), the line each row below demands. A second block re-runs the
# assignment/decomposition forms as standalone `cases/*.tks` on BOTH the own-native and the C route, so
# the two backends are witnessed to agree; the last block pins the runtime length-guard panic (ruling
# 5) on both routes. Multiple return synthesizes a by-value aggregate struct — there is no tuple type.

Feature: §9 F — the whole corpus on the own-native backend (main.tks project build)

  Scenario: parallel — `var a, b = 3, 7`, types inferred per position
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario parallel: ok"

  Scenario: parallel_reads_before_bind — every RHS value is read before any target is bound
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario parallel_reads_before_bind: ok"

  Scenario: shared_annotation — one shared `: u8` annotation over both targets
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario shared_annotation: ok"

  Scenario: decomp_skip — exact-length decomposition with a `_` discard
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario decomp_skip: ok"

  Scenario: decomp_rest — `var [h, .., p, q] = xs` head+tail across a skipped middle
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario decomp_rest: ok"

  Scenario: decomp_rest_zero_middle — a `..` that skips zero middle elements
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario decomp_rest_zero_middle: ok"

  Scenario: destructure_return — `var q, r = div(17, 5)` destructures a multiple return
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario destructure_return: ok"

  Scenario: destructure_return_skip — `var q, _ = div(20, 6)` discards a returned value
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario destructure_return_skip: ok"


Feature: §9 F — assignment/decomposition standalone cases, own-native and C route agree

  Scenario: parallel (own-native)
    Given source = "cases/parallel.tks"
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "parallel-ok"

  Scenario: parallel (C route)
    Given source = "cases/parallel.tks"
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "parallel-ok"

